---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { site } from '../data/site';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Terms of Service"
  description={`Terms of Service for ${site.companyName} (${site.brand}) — the conditions that govern your use of this website and the basis on which we provide product information and quotations.`}
>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <article class="legal">
        <h1>Terms of Service</h1>
        <p class="updated">Last updated: 25 October 2026</p>

        <p>
          These Terms of Service (&ldquo;Terms&rdquo;) govern your access to and use of{' '}
          <strong>{site.domain}</strong>, the website of <strong>{site.companyName}</strong>{' '}
          (&ldquo;{site.brand}&rdquo;, &ldquo;we&rdquo;, &ldquo;us&rdquo; or &ldquo;our&rdquo;). By accessing or
          using this website, you agree to be bound by these Terms. If you do not agree, please do not use the
          website.
        </p>
        <p>
          This website is a business-to-business resource. It presents product information, technical guidance
          and company details for professional buyers, importers and distributors of automotive filters. It is
          not a consumer online shop, and no binding sales contract is formed by using the website or
          submitting an inquiry.
        </p>

        <nav class="toc" aria-label="Terms contents">
          <strong>Contents</strong>
          <ol>
            <li>Acceptance of these Terms</li>
            <li>Who may use the website</li>
            <li>Nature of the website content</li>
            <li>Inquiries, quotations and orders</li>
            <li>Products, specifications and samples</li>
            <li>Pricing and payment</li>
            <li>Intellectual property</li>
            <li>Acceptable use</li>
            <li>Disclaimers and limitation of liability</li>
            <li>Indemnification</li>
            <li>Governing law and dispute resolution</li>
            <li>Changes to these Terms</li>
            <li>Contact us</li>
          </ol>
        </nav>

        <h2>1. Acceptance of these Terms</h2>
        <p>
          By accessing the website, you confirm that you have read and understood these Terms and that you agree
          to comply with them. We may update these Terms from time to time; the version published on this page
          will always be the current version. Your continued use of the website after changes are posted
          constitutes acceptance of the revised Terms.
        </p>

        <h2>2. Who may use the website</h2>
        <p>
          This website is intended for use by individuals acting in a professional or commercial capacity, such
          as buyers, importers, distributors, wholesalers and fleet operators. You must be at least 18 years of
          age to use the website and to submit information through it.
        </p>

        <h2>3. Nature of the website content</h2>
        <p>
          The content on this website — including product descriptions, technical articles, specifications,
          photographs, diagrams and selection guidance — is provided for <strong>general information and
          preliminary evaluation purposes only</strong>. It is not a binding offer of sale. While we take care
          to keep the content accurate and current, we do not guarantee that it is complete, error-free or
          up to date at all times.
        </p>
        <p>
          In particular, product specifications, dimensions, materials, filtration efficiency figures, packaging
          details, minimum order quantities, lead times and certifications shown on this website are indicative
          and subject to confirmation. The <strong>formal specification sheet and the confirmed proforma
          invoice</strong> issued by us for a specific order take precedence over any website content in the
          event of any inconsistency. Please see our <a href="/disclaimer/">Disclaimer</a> for further detail.
        </p>

        <h2>4. Inquiries, quotations and orders</h2>
        <p>
          Submitting an inquiry through our website or by email or messaging application does not create a
          contract and does not oblige us to supply any product. A quotation issued by us is an invitation to
          treat, not a binding offer, and is valid only for the period stated on it. An order becomes binding
          only when we confirm acceptance in writing, typically by means of a signed proforma invoice or
          purchase confirmation.
        </p>
        <p>
          You are responsible for ensuring that the information you provide to us — including OE numbers,
          vehicle types, target markets, quantities and any technical requirements — is accurate and complete.
          We rely on that information when preparing quotations and manufacturing products.
        </p>

        <h2>5. Products, specifications and samples</h2>
        <p>
          Our products are manufactured to the specifications we agree with you in writing. Where a
          pre-production sample is required, we will provide it for your approval; you should verify dimensions,
          fitment, media, seal and packaging before approving mass production. Once a sample is approved, we
          will manufacture the confirmed order against that approval.
        </p>
        <p>
          Product specifications are subject to change without notice as part of continuous improvement, provided
          that any change to a confirmed order is agreed with you in writing before production. Photographs and
          images on this website are for illustration and may not reflect the exact appearance of the current
          production version.
        </p>
        <h3>5.1 Warranty and after-sales</h3>
        <p>
          Warranty terms are set out in the sales contract or proforma invoice for each order. As a general
          reference, our products carry a warranty period of one year from delivery, excluding vulnerable and
          consumable parts; specific terms and exclusions are confirmed with the salesperson for the product in
          question. After-sales support is provided in accordance with the agreed terms; where on-site support
          is required, any travel, accommodation and related costs are agreed separately between the parties.
          Nothing on this website constitutes a warranty, and no warranty is created except as expressly set out
          in a signed written agreement.
        </p>

        <h2>6. Pricing and payment</h2>
        <p>
          Prices are quoted on a case-by-case basis and may be expressed in a currency agreed between the
          parties. Unless otherwise stated in writing, payment terms follow the arrangement common in
          international trade: an initial deposit to confirm the order, with the balance payable before
          shipment. Specific payment terms, delivery terms (such as Incoterms) and the allocation of freight,
          insurance and duties are agreed in the proforma invoice or sales contract for each order. Unless a
          credit arrangement has been agreed in writing, production typically begins after receipt of the agreed
          deposit, and the balance is payable before release of the shipment.
        </p>

        <h2>7. Intellectual property</h2>
        <p>
          The website and its content, including text, articles, graphics, logos, data tables and the overall
          design, are owned by or licensed to {site.companyName} and are protected by applicable intellectual
          property laws. You may view and print pages for your own internal business use, but you may not
          reproduce, republish, distribute, modify or commercially exploit any content without our prior written
          consent. The <strong>{site.brand}</strong> name and associated marks are our trade marks; nothing on
          this website grants you any licence to use them.
        </p>

        <h2>8. Acceptable use</h2>
        <p>You agree not to:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Use the website in any way that is unlawful, fraudulent or harmful;</li>
          <li>Attempt to gain unauthorised access to the website, its servers or any connected systems;</li>
          <li>Introduce or transmit malicious code, viruses or harmful material;</li>
          <li>Scrape, crawl or harvest content in a manner that places unreasonable load on our systems or breaches these Terms;</li>
          <li>Misrepresent your identity or your affiliation with any person or organisation;</li>
          <li>Use the website to send unsolicited communications or to infringe the rights of others.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>9. Disclaimers and limitation of liability</h2>
        <p>
          To the fullest extent permitted by law, the website and its content are provided on an &ldquo;as
          is&rdquo; and &ldquo;as available&rdquo; basis without warranties of any kind, whether express or
          implied, including but not limited to warranties of merchantability, fitness for a particular purpose,
          accuracy and non-infringement.
        </p>
        <p>
          To the fullest extent permitted by law, {site.companyName} and its officers, employees and agents
          shall not be liable for any indirect, incidental, special, consequential or punitive damages, or for
          any loss of profits, revenue, data or goodwill, arising out of or in connection with your use of the
          website or your reliance on its content, even if advised of the possibility of such damages. Nothing in
          these Terms excludes or limits liability that cannot be excluded or limited under applicable law.
        </p>
        <p>
          Because product specifications are reference in nature, you must not rely on website content as a
          substitute for a formal specification sheet or for your own verification of fitment and compatibility.
        </p>

        <h2>10. Indemnification</h2>
        <p>
          You agree to indemnify and hold harmless {site.companyName} and its officers, employees and agents
          from and against any claims, liabilities, damages, losses and expenses (including reasonable legal
          fees) arising out of or in connection with your breach of these Terms or your misuse of the website.
        </p>

        <h2>11. Governing law and dispute resolution</h2>
        <p>
          These Terms are governed by and construed in accordance with the laws of the People&rsquo;s Republic of
          China, without regard to its conflict-of-law principles. Any dispute arising out of or in connection
          with these Terms or your use of the website shall first be attempted to be resolved amicably through
          negotiation. Where a dispute cannot be resolved by negotiation, it shall be submitted to the competent
          court having jurisdiction over the location of {site.companyName}, unless mandatory law provides
          otherwise.
        </p>
        <p>
          If any provision of these Terms is held to be invalid or unenforceable, that provision shall be
          severed and the remaining provisions shall continue in full force and effect. These Terms, together
          with our Privacy Policy and Disclaimer, constitute the entire agreement between you and us regarding
          your use of the website and supersede any prior agreements on that subject.
        </p>

        <h2>12. Changes to these Terms</h2>
        <p>
          We may revise these Terms at any time by updating this page. The &ldquo;Last updated&rdquo; date at the
          top of this page indicates when the current version took effect. It is your responsibility to review
          these Terms periodically.
        </p>

        <h2>13. Contact us</h2>
        <p>Questions about these Terms should be directed to:</p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Email:</strong> <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a></li>
          <li><strong>WhatsApp:</strong> {site.whatsapp}</li>
          <li><strong>Address:</strong> {site.address}</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          Related documents: <a href="/privacy/">Privacy Policy</a> &middot; <a href="/disclaimer/">Disclaimer</a> &middot; <a href="/cookies/">Cookie Policy</a>.
        </p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
